course: dictionary
lesson: 5805
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Maggot has two: first, the young form of a fly; second, an old-fashioned rude name for a worthless person. To find the right meaning, look at the words around it and ask: is this sentence about nature, science or flies, or about a person?
explain: «In Waitomo Caves in New Zealand, glowworms, which are fly larvae (young flies, like maggots), glow to lure insects into sticky threads.» The clues are fly larvae and young flies, so here maggot means the young form of a fly. The brackets help you: they tell you that a maggot is like a larva.
explain: The insult meaning is old-fashioned, so you will meet it less often. A sentence that uses it will describe a person, not eggs or rotting food. Always swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: A maggot is the young form of a fly, called a larva.
fact: A maggot hatches from an egg and feeds on rotting food or dead animals.
fact: A fly's life cycle goes: egg, larva (maggot), pupa, adult fly.
fact: Maggots help clean up nature by eating rotting things.
fact: «Maggot» has an old-fashioned meaning: a rude name for a worthless person.
exercise: «In Waitomo Caves, glowworms are fly larvae (young flies, like maggots).» What is a maggot in this sentence? | A type of cave | *A young fly | A kind of starry sky | A rude name for a person
exercise: Which stage of a fly's life cycle is the maggot? | Egg | *Larva | Adult fly | Pupa
exercise: An old story calls a cruel lord «a maggot». What does this mean? | *A rude name for a worthless person | A tiny piece of food | A kind of fishing bait | A small, pale fly
test: What do maggots feed on? | Fresh flowers | Clean water | *Rotting food or dead animals | Sand and stones
test: Which comes first in a fly's life cycle? | Maggot | Adult fly | *Egg | Pupa
exam: In «crawling with maggots», what does maggots mean? | A crowd of happy children | *Many young flies feeding on rotting food | Glowing lights in a cave | Bright stars in a sky
